prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior animated mathematical visualization engineer. Output only one complete ASCII HTML file using MathBox. No Markdown fences or prose outside the source.
  text: |-
    Create a dense MathBox visualization of the gradient field for z=x^2-y^2. Show the saddle surface, contour traces on the base plane, vectors representing grad z=(2*x,-2*y), and an animated point moving along a steepest-ascent path. Include an explanatory HTML panel with the derivative derivation.

    Requirements: use area, interval or array data nodes as appropriate, vector display, surface display, clock-driven animation, bounded sample counts, axis labels with units, and a camera path or controls that keep the saddle visible. Include WebGL fallback status text.
  provider_options:
    temperature: 0.2
    max_tokens: 8192
output:
  text_format: html
  artifact_kind: mathbox-html
  formats:
  - format: html
  - format: png
  - format: webgl
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "YAML parses and required schema 0.4 fields are present."
  - "HTML is complete, ASCII-only, and uses MathBox data/display primitives for surface, contours, vectors, and animation."
  - "Math correctness covers saddle equation, gradient vector components, contour levels, and steepest-ascent direction."
  - "Notation validity covers equation text, derivative notation, labels, units, and explanatory panel."
  - "Renderability covers nonblank first frame, bounded sample counts, animation loop, and WebGL fallback."
  - "Labels and units identify x, y, z, gradient vectors, contour plane, path point, and time."
  - "Domain edge cases cover dense vector clutter, per-frame allocation, camera clipping, WebGL failure, and resize."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII HTML file with no Markdown wrapper."
    - "The file uses valid MathBox scene graph, data nodes, display nodes, and animation constructs."
    - "The source documents dependency versions, run, and capture expectations."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Surface, contour traces, gradient vectors, animated point, derivation panel, labels, and fallback are all present."
    - "MathBox remains the primary rendering surface for 3D mathematical structure."
    - "The derivative derivation agrees with the rendered field."
  - name: Visual/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "Dense layers are readable through hierarchy, opacity, color, and sampling."
    - "Animation supports understanding without distracting or obscuring labels."
    - "The first camera view frames the full saddle and vector field."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles vector density, resize, WebGL failure, and low-power GPUs."
    - "Uses bounded animation and avoids unbounded allocations."
    - "Documents version and performance constraints."
  pass_conditions:
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, Visual/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "Score is 80 or higher out of 100 with no critical failure in math correctness, notation validity, or renderability."
  - "The artifact presents a dense but readable MathBox gradient-field derivation."
  - "Domain edge cases and performance safeguards are represented."
